From 1398cc90e2334a207defd4c2f80f1970418a320c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Penkava <mpenkava1337@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:58:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hdmv: end button command execution after a link command

LinkPI / LinkMK only queued the jump and execution continued with the
next button command. Discs put a fallback after the link, e.g.
"LinkMK r0; JumpTitle 1" in a chapter menu, so the jump to the chapter
was immediately replaced by restarting the title.

Terminate the button commands after queuing the link, like BREAK does.
---
 src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c b/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c
index e1b5a817..eac09c1f 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c
@@ -685,6 +685,9 @@ static int _link_at(HDMV_VM *p, int playitem, int playmark)
         _queue_event(p, HDMV_EVENT_PLAY_PM, playmark);
     }
 
+    /* link commands end the execution of button commands (like BREAK) */
+    p->pc = 1 << 17;
+
     return 0;
 }
 
